Good to know: Next.js also allows the file to be named .postcssrc.js.

Do not use require() to import the PostCSS Plugins. Plugins must be provided as strings.

Good to know: If your postcss.config.js needs to support other non-Next.js tools in the same project, you must use the interoperable object-based format instead:module.exports = {
  plugins: {
    'postcss-flexbugs-fixes': {},
    'postcss-preset-env': {
      autoprefixer: {
        flexbox: 'no-2009',
      },
      stage: 3,
      features: {
        'custom-properties': false,
      },
    },
  },
}
